  "description": "Simply put, the Airwolf does everything better and makes everything easier. You name it, wheelies, bunny hops, grinds, spins. All easier on the Airwolf than any other frame that we’ve ever ridden. This is the future face of fixed gear freestyle and it’s still plenty of fun to run around on and use as a regular everyday bike.\n\nThe Airwolf was designed to be used with our Dropout fork.\n\nFrame: 100% full 4130 ChroMoly steel. Double butted down, top, and seat tubes. Top and down tube gussets at the head tube.\n\nFork: It’s just a frame bro, but it’s designed to utilize the Dropout fork.\n\n14mm Dropouts: The future is now\n\nFreestyle Geometry: The new style, double peg combatible BB height, super short chainstays, plenty of barspin clearance\n\nE.D. Finish: The entire bike is E.D. coated inside and out. E.D. coating not only improves the quality and durability of the paint, but is the best rust proofing agent going. With the E.D. coating there is no need to Frame Saver the bike, it’s already done for you.",
